# description : This .audit is designed against the CIS SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 15 STIG Benchmark v1.0.0
#
#<ui_metadata>
#<display_name>CIS SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 15 STIG v1.0.0 CAT III</display_name>
#<spec>
#  <type>CIS</type>
#  <name>SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 15 STIG</name>
#  <profile>CAT III</profile>
#  <version>1.0.0</version>
#  <link>https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23779</link>
#</spec>
#<labels>agent,suse_linux_15</labels>
#<benchmark_refs>800-53,800-53r5,CAT,CCI,LEVEL,Rule-ID,STIG-ID,Vuln-ID</benchmark_refs>
#<variables>
#  <variable>
#    <name>PLATFORM_VERSION</name>
#    <default>15</default>
#    <description>SUSE Version</description>
#    <info>SUSE Version</info>
#    <value_type>STRING</value_type>
#  </variable>
#  <variable>
#    <name>REMOTE_AUDIT_LOG_SERVER</name>
#    <default>10.0.21.1</default>
#    <description>Remote audit log server</description>
#    <info>The IP address or FQDN of the central log server for as it appears in /etc/audisp/audisp-remote.conf.</info>
#    <value_type>STRING</value_type>
#  </variable>
#  <variable>
#    <name>AUDIT_MOUNT</name>
#    <default>/var/log/audit</default>
#    <description>Audit log data partition</description>
#    <info>The separate file system for audit log data</info>
#    <value_type>STRING</value_type>
#  </variable>
#  <variable>
#    <name>AIDE_CONF</name>
#    <default>/etc/aide.conf</default>
#    <description>AIDE Configuration File</description>
#    <info>Full path to the aide.conf file.</info>
#    <value_type>UNIX_FILE_PATH</value_type>
#  </variable>
#  <variable>
#    <name>HOME_MOUNT</name>
#    <default>/home</default>
#    <description>User home partition</description>
#    <info>The separate file system for non-privileged local interactive user home directories</info>
#    <value_type>STRING</value_type>
#  </variable>
#</variables>
#</ui_metadata>

<check_type:"Unix">

<if>
  <condition type:"AND">
    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "SUSE Linux 15 is installed - VERSION"
      file        : "/etc/os-release"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*VERSION[\\s]*="
      expect      : "^[\\s]*VERSION[\\s]*=\"[\\s]*@PLATFORM_VERSION@"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
      description : "SUSE Linux 15 is installed - NAME"
      file        : "/etc/os-release"
      regex       : "^[\\s]*NAME[\\s]*="
      expect      : "^[\\s]*NAME[\\s]*=\"[\\s]*SLES[\\s]*\"$"
    </custom_item>
  </condition>

  <then>
    <report type:"PASSED">
      description : "CIS_SUSE_Linux_Enterprise_Server_15_STIG_v1.0.0_CAT_III.audit from CIS SUSE Linux Enterprise Server 15 STIG v1.0.0"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23779"
      show_output : YES
    </report>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.109 SLES-15-030060"
      info        : "The SUSE operating system must generate audit records for all uses of the ssh-keysign command.

GROUP ID: V-234905
RULE ID: SV-234905r958412

Reconstruction of harmful events or forensic analysis is not possible if audit records do not contain enough information.

At a minimum, the organization must audit the full-text recording of privileged commands. The organization must maintain audit trails in sufficient detail to reconstruct events to determine the cause and impact of compromise.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000037-GPOS-00015, SRG-OS-000042-GPOS-00020, SRG-OS-000062-GPOS-00031, SRG-OS-000392-GPOS-00172, SRG-OS-000462-GPOS-00206, SRG-OS-000471-GPOS-00215"
      solution    : "Configure the SUSE operating system to generate an audit record for all uses of the \"ssh-keysign\" command.

Add or update the following rules in the \"/etc/audit/rules.d/audit.rules\" file:

-a always,exit -F path=/usr/lib/ssh/ssh-keysign -F perm=x -F auid>=1000 -F auid!=4294967295 -k privileged-ssh-keysign

To reload the rules file, restart the audit daemon

sudo systemctl restart auditd.service

or issue the following command:

sudo augenrules --load"
      reference   : "800-171|3.3.1,800-171|3.3.2,800-171|3.7.5,800-171r3|03.03.02a.,800-171r3|03.03.03a.,800-171r3|03.07.05,800-53|AU-3,800-53|AU-12a.,800-53|AU-12c.,800-53|MA-4(1),800-53r5|AU-3a.,800-53r5|AU-12a.,800-53r5|AU-12c.,800-53r5|MA-4(1),CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000130,CCI|CCI-000169,CCI|CCI-000172,CCI|CCI-002884,CN-L3|7.1.2.3(a),CN-L3|7.1.2.3(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(a),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(b),CN-L3|7.1.3.3(c),CN-L3|8.1.3.5(a),CN-L3|8.1.3.5(b),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(a),CN-L3|8.1.4.3(b),CSF|DE.CM-1,CSF|DE.CM-3,CSF|DE.CM-7,CSF|PR.MA-2,CSF|PR.PT-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-01,CSF2.0|DE.CM-03,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-04,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(b),ISO-27001-2022|A.5.28,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.15,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.16,ISO/IEC-27001|A.12.4.1,ITSG-33|AU-3,ITSG-33|AU-12a.,ITSG-33|AU-12c.,ITSG-33|MA-4(1),LEVEL|3M,NESA|T2.3.4,NESA|T3.6.2,NESA|T3.6.5,NESA|T3.6.6,NIAv2|AM34a,NIAv2|AM34b,NIAv2|AM34c,NIAv2|AM34d,NIAv2|AM34e,NIAv2|AM34f,NIAv2|AM34g,NIAv2|SM8,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.1,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.2,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.3,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.4,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.5,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|10.3.6,PCI-DSSv4.0|10.2.2,QCSC-v1|3.2,QCSC-v1|5.2.2,QCSC-v1|6.2,QCSC-v1|8.2.1,QCSC-v1|13.2,Rule-ID|SV-234905r958412_rule,STIG-ID|SLES-15-030060,SWIFT-CSCv1|6.4,TBA-FIISB|45.1.1,TBA-FIISB|45.2.3,Vuln-ID|V-234905"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23779"
      cmd         : "/sbin/auditctl -l | /bin/grep -w '/usr/lib/ssh/ssh-keysign'"
      expect      : "^\\s*-a\\s+(always,exit|exit,always)(\\s+-S\\s+all)?\\s+-F\\s+path=/usr/lib/ssh/ssh-keysign\\s+(-F\\s+perm=([rwa]*x[rwa]*)\\s+)?-F\\s+auid>=1000\\s+-F\\s+auid!=(4294967295|-1|unset)(\\s+(-k\\s+|-F\\s+key=)\\S+)*\\s*$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.11 SLES-15-010110"
      info        : "The SUSE operating system must utilize vlock to allow for session locking.

GROUP ID: V-234811
RULE ID: SV-234811r1009610

A session lock is a temporary action taken when a user stops work and moves away from the immediate physical vicinity of the information system but does not want to log out because of the temporary nature of the absence.

The session lock is implemented at the point where session activity can be determined.

Regardless of where the session lock is determined and implemented, once invoked, the session lock must remain in place until the user reauthenticates. No other activity aside from reauthentication must unlock the system.

Satisfies: SRG-OS-000028-GPOS-00009, SRG-OS-000030-GPOS-00011, SRG-OS-000031-GPOS-00012"
      solution    : "Allow users to lock the console by installing the \"kbd\" package using zypper:

sudo zypper install kbd"
      reference   : "800-171|3.1.10,800-171r3|03.01.10,800-171r3|03.01.10a.,800-171r3|03.01.10b.,800-53|AC-11,800-53|AC-11a.,800-53|AC-11b.,800-53|AC-11(1),800-53r5|AC-11a.,800-53r5|AC-11b.,800-53r5|AC-11(1),CAT|III,CCI|CCI-000056,CCI|CCI-000057,CCI|CCI-000058,CCI|CCI-000060,CN-L3|8.1.4.1(b),GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),HIPAA|164.312(a)(2)(iii),ISO-27001-2022|A.7.7,ISO-27001-2022|A.8.1,ISO/IEC-27001|A.11.2.8,ITSG-33|AC-11,ITSG-33|AC-11a.,ITSG-33|AC-11b.,ITSG-33|AC-11(1),LEVEL|3M,NESA|T2.3.8,NESA|T2.3.9,NIAv2|AM23a,NIAv2|AM23b,NIAv2|AM23c,NIAv2|AM23d,NIAv2|AM23e,PCI-DSSv3.2.1|8.1.8,PCI-DSSv4.0|8.2.8,Rule-ID|SV-234811r1009610_rule,STIG-ID|SLES-15-010110,Vuln-ID|V-234811"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23779"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/zypper search --installed-only --match-exact --provides vlock"
      expect      : "^[\\s]*i[\\s]*\|[\\s]*vlock[\\s]*"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.111 SLES-15-030080"
